[0m$ [0mcd /home/agent/projects/netscript/wave7-billing-steer2 && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'
Mount SemicircularGauge on the run console as the run-progress hero

The gauge existed and was registered in the gallery, but no product route
rendered it. It now anchors /runs/[id] as a five-band WidgetCard: header with
a pill action, the 180° arc as the body, and hairline footer columns beneath.

Three things the mount had to settle, all found by rendering it rather than
by reading it:

- Geometry is item counts, not money. A run's only honest denominator is the
  item: settled, excepted, or open. Money is what the reader is then told
  about that shape — the centre carries the issued figure, the footer carries
  what each outcome is worth.
- `sumMoney` joins lib/money, so the footer's per-outcome amounts are added on
  digit strings with BigInt rather than through a float. A column footer in a
  billing product is a statement, and M8 keeps that arithmetic out of
  components.
- An empty group is a real zero, not absence. No item failed means "$0.00 was
  excepted"; items whose amount was never computed means the em dash. Only a
  group whose members were all unmeasured earns `null`.

Also in this commit:

- `formatMoneyWithCurrency` — `formatMoney` deliberately omits the symbol so
  MoneyText can render it as a spaced prefix element, but a gauge centre and a
  footer column take a string, and gluing `$` on by hand at a call site is how
  `100.00USD` happens.
- Footer direction is a domain fact per column (issued towards us, excepted
  away), downgraded to flat at zero and to absent when unmeasured — a column
  reading $0.00 is not a movement in either direction.
- `1 item` / `2 items` in the legend.
EOF
