[0m$ [0mcd /home/agent/projects/netscript/wave7-billing-steer2 && git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'
Mount ComparisonAreaChart on the run console over computed vs prior

The chart existed and was registered, but the only place it rendered was the
gallery, over fixture data. It now sits beside the run-progress gauge on
/runs/[id] and plots the contract's own pair: each item's computedTotal
against the priorTotal recorded for the same subscription.

That pair is not a benchmark or a projection. AMOUNT_DELTA exceptions are
decided from exactly these two numbers, so the comparison layer is the other
half of a decision the console already asks the operator to make.

Decisions the mount forced, each found by rendering rather than by reading:

- An item is plotted only when it carries both amounts. A series with holes
  draws a line through values it does not have; what could not be compared
  becomes a footer column instead of a gap in the curve.
- Both period totals are summed over the same population — the compared items
  only. Comparing "everything this run" against "everything last period"
  would report a change in item count as a change in price.
- A dense series labels its ends only. Every point keeps its own hover
  readout, so nothing becomes unreachable; several hundred names under one
  axis would only overlap into a smudge.
- With no prior period the delta chip reads absent, not flat. There is nothing
  to compare, and holding steady is a claim about a measurement that was made.
EOF
