Mount DeltaChip on the runs index against the preceding run

The chip existed and was registered, but the only deltas in the product were
the gallery's fixture strings. The runs index now states the latest run's total
against the run before it, because "is the book growing?" is a comparison and
a bare figure invites the reader to supply the trend from memory.

One run is not a flat movement. With nothing to measure against, the chip
renders absent rather than +0.0% — a run that has not been compared has not
held steady.

The derivation moved into lib/money as `movement()`, shared with the
run-comparison chart rather than restated there. It is the partner to `ratio`,
and they part company on exactly this case: `ratio` answers "what fraction", a
movement answers "which way and by how much", and a fraction of nothing is
absent rather than zero.
