[0m$ [0mcd /home/agent/projects/netscript/wave7-billing-steer2 && git add apps/ledgerline-web/components/ui/segmented-control.tsx "apps/ledgerline-web/routes/invoices/(_components)/invoice-list.tsx" && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'
Mount SegmentedControl on the invoice status filter

The filter was a row of bare links carrying `aria-current` and nothing else,
so the selected status was announced to assistive tech and never shown to
anyone. The segmented control fills the selected cell, which is the point of
the control (C4): selection is a fill, not a border and not a colour.

The runs filter keeps its plain link row. It has ten cells against the
invoices filter's six, and a control sized for `1D 1W 1M 3M 1Y` stops
describing a range once it is asked to hold ten — that filter needs grouping
first, not restyling. Its active state is invisible for the same reason this
one was, and that is recorded rather than fixed here.

Link mode also gains `clientNav`. Every other filter link in the app opts into
Fresh's client-side navigation, and a range that lives in the URL is usually a
filter: reloading the whole page to change a query parameter is a slower
version of the same navigation.
EOF
